source_units.display_text:
We all, like sheep, have gone astray;
each person has strayed in his own way.
And the Lord delivered him over to our sins.

And I will give the wicked in exchange for his burial,
and the rich in exchange for his death;
for he committed no iniquity,
nor was deceit found in his mouth.

from the toil of his soul,
to show him light and fashion him with understanding,
to justify the righteous one who serves many well;
and he will bear their sins.

Therefore he will inherit many,
and will divide the spoils of the mighty;
for his soul was delivered to death,
and he was numbered among the lawless.
And he bore the sins of many,
and for their sins he was delivered up.

You who thirst, go to the water;
and you who have no silver, go and buy wine and rich food,
and drink without silver or price.

let the ungodly forsake his ways,
and the lawless man his counsels;
and let him return to the Lord, and he will receive mercy;
for He will abundantly forgive your sins.

so it will be with My word, whatever goes out from My mouth:
it will certainly not return until all that I have willed is accomplished;
and I will prosper your ways and My commandments.

For you will go out in gladness, and in joy you will be taught;
for the mountains and the hills will leap, welcoming you with joy,
and all the trees of the field will clap their branches.
